@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+## Context
+
+`src/json-patch.ts` has private `isObject`, `setMember` and `clone` helpers that handle `__proto__` safely.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- New module `src/json-merge-patch.ts`, recursive `mergePatch(target, patch)` following the RFC pseudocode. It builds a new result rather than mutating.
+- Reuse the helpers by exporting `isObject`, `setMember` and `clone` from `json-patch.ts` instead of duplicating them.
+- A non-object patch returns `clone(patch)`. Object patch values are merged against `{}` when the target member is not an object, which drops nested nulls as the RFC prescribes.
+- Own-member checks use `Object.hasOwn`; never plain property access on `__proto__`.
+- No errors are thrown: every JSON value is a valid patch.
